---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="A plain-language overview of the privacy boundaries in the PAUSE AI app and this public status website."
>
  <section class="page-hero shell" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy overview · reviewed 11 July 2026</p>
    <h1 id="privacy-title">A boundary should respect yours.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      PAUSE is designed to reduce interruption without becoming another place that reads, replies, or follows
      you around. This page explains the product and website boundaries in plain language.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell privacy-at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
      <h2 id="glance-title">Local first. Cloud by choice. No hidden website tracker.</h2>
    </div>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>Notification action</dt>
        <dd>Deterministic policy on the Android device stays authoritative.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Cloud AI</dt>
        <dd>Off by default and used only after an explicit account preference.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Website analytics</dt>
        <dd>None added by PAUSE. GitHub Pages still handles ordinary web requests.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="shell privacy-layers" aria-label="Privacy boundaries">
    <article aria-labelledby="app-data-title">
      <div class="layer-label"><span>01</span> Android app</div>
      <div class="layer-copy">
        <h2 id="app-data-title">The app sees only what you authorize</h2>
        <p>
          Android notification access and monitored-app selection are explicit setup steps. PAUSE uses those
          signals to broker delivery; it does not send messages or auto-reply inside other apps.
        </p>
        <p>
          Active boundaries, rules, exceptions, and private vault state are handled locally. SecureStore protects
          sensitive device credentials, while SQLite keeps local behavior available when the network is not.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article aria-labelledby="cloud-data-title">
      <div class="layer-label"><span>02</span> Account and cloud</div>
      <div class="layer-copy">
        <h2 id="cloud-data-title">Cloud processing has separate gates</h2>
        <p>
          Signing in enables owner-scoped synchronization such as account presets. Supabase Row Level Security
          limits cloud rows to the authenticated owner. Cloud AI is a separate preference, defaults to off, and
          sends eligible content through authenticated Edge Functions only when enabled.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI output is advisory. Edge Functions keep provider credentials off-device, and deterministic policy
          decides the final notification action if the provider is unavailable, uncertain, or disabled.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article aria-labelledby="control-title">
      <div class="layer-label"><span>03</span> Your controls</div>
      <div class="layer-copy">
        <h2 id="control-title">Retention and deletion are visible actions</h2>
        <p>
          Notification-preview retention is configurable. Zero-hour retention prevents preview text from being
          retained in cloud records and excludes it from digest guidance. Turning Cloud AI off stops new optional
          AI processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloud-data deletion and account deletion cover synchronized records, including saved boundary presets.
          The public health check tests deletion with dedicated synthetic accounts; it never uses a visitor account.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article aria-labelledby="website-title">
      <div class="layer-label"><span>04</span> This website</div>
      <div class="layer-copy">
        <h2 id="website-title">Static and tracker-free by PAUSE—not invisible to its host</h2>
        <p>
          PAUSE adds no analytics, advertising pixels, marketing cookies, contact form, account system, or
          browser-side Supabase client to this site. Filtering the Updates page happens in your browser and does
          not send the selection anywhere.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like an ordinary web host, GitHub may receive and process request
          data such as an IP address, browser or device headers, requested URL, and timestamps to deliver and
          secure the service. GitHub controls that hosting activity under its
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noreferrer">
            General Privacy Statement <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="shell evidence-note" aria-labelledby="evidence-note-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Public status data</p>
      <h2 id="evidence-note-title">Evidence is deliberately narrow</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>
        GitHub Actions runs a dedicated synthetic health account away from visitors. The published snapshot is
        allowlisted to component state, evidence type, safe summary, timestamps, optional latency, and approved
        public error codes.
      </p>
      <p>
        It excludes email addresses, user IDs, tokens, provider responses, exception text, notification content,
        and secret values. “Live,” “daily,” and “release” describe evidence freshness—not a contractual uptime or
        privacy guarantee.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="shell overview-note">
    This is a product privacy overview, not a substitute for a formal legal notice. It will be updated as the
    application, hosting, or data paths change.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    max-width: 980px;
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem) clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    max-width: 12ch;
  }

  .privacy-at-a-glance {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .section-heading {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .privacy-at-a-glance dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .privacy-at-a-glance dl > div {
    min-height: 180px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .privacy-at-a-glance dl > div:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }

  dt,
  .layer-label {
    color: var(--color-privacy);
    font: 0.7rem/1.45 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  dd {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    color: var(--color-soft);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .privacy-layers {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .privacy-layers article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, 0.45fr) minmax(0, 1.55fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .privacy-layers article:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .layer-label span {
    display: inline-grid;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
    place-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .layer-copy h2 {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .layer-copy p,
  .evidence-note p {
    max-width: 70ch;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.78;
  }

  .layer-copy a {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--color-calm);
  }

  .evidence-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr);
    gap: 2rem 3rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-privacy) 8%, var(--color-surface));
  }

  .overview-note {
    margin-block: 1.2rem clamp(6rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    color: var(--color-dim);
    font: 0.72rem/1.7 var(--font-mono);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .privacy-at-a-glance dl,
    .privacy-layers article,
    .evidence-note {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .privacy-at-a-glance dl > div {
      min-height: 0;
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    }

    .privacy-at-a-glance dl > div:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    dd {
      margin-top: 1.2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
